| 15 | [Install and verify the complete workflow across platforms](15-verify-packaged-workflow-across-platforms.md) | AFK | 14 | US-1, US-2, US-3, US-4, US-5, US-6, US-7, US-8 |

Only issue 1 is initially ready. Issues 1–8 form the first execution path; 9, 10, 11, and 12 may proceed in parallel after 8. Issue 13 joins 10–12; 14 joins 9 and 13; 15 follows 14. See [graph.json](graph.json) for the same machine-readable graph.

## Shared implementation contracts

These are proposed decisions for consistent implementation, not undocumented existing APIs.

- Use strict TypeScript and named exports. `src/plugin.ts` assembles adapters and commands; `src/core/orchestrator.ts` owns phase transitions.
- `src/opencode/adapter.ts` is the only OpenCode SDK boundary. Establish `OpenCodeAdapter` with `dispatchJob`, `cancelJob`, `requestUserInput`, and `publishStatus`. Bind every operation to explicit session/workspace/run identity. Preserve configured permissions.
- `src/core/types.ts` defines `RunRecord`, `RunEvent`, `JobEnvelope`, and `JobResult`. Jobs carry role, run ID, issue ID if applicable, attempt, session/workspace, input revisions and base commit. Events have ordered sequence IDs; outputs cannot override approval state.
- `src/state/run-store.ts` exports `openRunStore` and `RunStore` for atomic versioned snapshots, append-only events and operation intent/result journaling. Use a Git-common-directory repository identity and canonical store/lock, not one scheduler per worktree.
- Commands use stable IDs, lifecycle phase, executable/args, cwd, timeout and explicit platform/env references. Execution results distinguish completed exit status, timeout, cancellation and permission denial.
- `src/execution/validation.ts` exports `validateCandidate` and `ValidationSummary`. Results identify the exact candidate SHA and command revision; omissions remain separate from pass/fail.
- `tests/helpers/project.ts` exports `createTestProject`; `tests/helpers/fake-opencode.ts` exports `createFakeOpenCode`. Use real temporary Git repositories with initial commits, controllable agent responses, an injectable clock and portable fixture processes.
- Issue 1 establishes scripts `typecheck`, `lint`, `build`, `test`, `test:browser`, and `test:smoke`. Deterministic tests use `bun:test`. Browser tests use Playwright once added by issue 10. Live OpenCode smoke tests are explicitly gated and report skipped status when unavailable.
- Every behavior change uses TDD. A testable bug repair begins with a regression test. Record exceptions only for changes with no meaningful behavioral test.

### Parallel review contract (issues 11 and 12)

Both branches accept a structurally identical snapshot:

```typescript
type ReviewSnapshot = {
  runId: string;
  round: number;
  commit: string;
  prdRevision: string;
  graphRevision: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
};
```

Both return their role, reviewed commit and round, outcome (`passed`, `findings`, or `unverified`), findings and evidence references. The functional role additionally returns criterion results and unavailable-attempt evidence. Issue 11 owns shared `src/review/types.ts`; issue 12 may use a local structural contract without importing the not-yet-merged branch. Issue 13 consolidates these interfaces. This preserves the approved independent dependencies.

### Integration and retry invariants

1. Three **total issue attempts**, including the initial attempt; TDD red-stage failures do not consume them.
2. Three **total final review rounds**; repair tasks separately have three issue attempts.
3. Functional-review infrastructure retries are bounded separately and cannot create extra review rounds.
4. Only hung validation checks are skipped. Setup/readiness timeouts, completed failures, cancellation and permission denial are not skipped checks.
5. The check skip list is run-local and never modifies approved command JSON. All checks skipped permits continued work with missing validation reported.
6. Never advance integration before checking the exact candidate. Never modify the target branch or publish automatically.
7. Remove successful issue worktrees only after integration; retain failures and cleanup evidence.
8. Restore state on restart, but require an explicit resume instruction. Stale or duplicate events cannot repeat side effects.

## Validation and completion

Every ticket has exact planned validation commands and an independently demonstrable scenario. Commands are **not presently available**: no code has been implemented in this documentation task. Do not claim checks passed until they actually run in the implementation.

Keep the PRD unchanged unless the user separately requests changes. Do not create GitHub issues, publish a package, or start execution merely because this backlog exists.

## Source references

- [PRD](../../PRD.md)
- [OpenCode plugin documentation](https://opencode.ai/docs/plugins/) — plugin context and hooks; compatibility must be pinned in issue 1.
- [OpenCode SDK documentation](https://opencode.ai/docs/sdk/) — session/client integration reference.
- [OpenCode commands documentation](https://opencode.ai/docs/commands/) — supported command configuration.

Documentation consulted 2026-10-14. These references are inputs to the explicit compatibility slice; no unverified SDK call signature is asserted by the backlog.

